        <fullName>EmployeeExpenseManagement_16jak000001jV3t</fullName>
        <canEscalate>false</canEscalate>
        <description>Manage all expense-related operations, including querying expense policies, viewing expense statuses, creating and submitting expense reports.</description>
        <developerName>EmployeeExpenseManagement_16jak000001jV3t</developerName>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>If the user asks to see the allowed expense items or categories, you MUST call the `GetExpenseItems` action and show user the list of allowed expense items and categories grouped by their respective category. When presenting the information, include &quot;Connected with Workday&quot; as part of the response content.</description>
            <developerName>handle_expense_item_catalog</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>handle_expense_item_catalog</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>0</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>if the user ask to see the past reports, call the action `GetPastExpenseReports` to fetch the list of past expense reports associated with the employee. When presenting the reports, include &quot;Connected with Workday&quot; as part of the response content.
 
 Display a summary for each report including:
   - Report Number, Report Date, Report Status, Total Amount
   - Expense details (if available)

 Allow the user to select a report for further details.</description>
            <developerName>fetch_past_expense_reports</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>fetch_past_expense_reports</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>1</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Initiate a conversation to create an expense report. An expense report can have multiple expenses, which must be added to the `ExpenseDetailsList` parameter of the `SubmitExpenseReport` action.
  First, call the `GetExpenseItems` action  to fetch the list of allowed expense items and categories.
  Then collect the following details for &quot;SubmitExpenseReport&quot;
  - Report Name
  - Report Date
  - Cost Center 
  - ExpenseDetailsList -  This property is of list type of APEX type &quot;@apexClassType/sfdc_employee_service__GenerateExpenseDetails&quot;. It can have 1 or more entries. Ask user to provide input for it. Below are the properties of &quot;@apexClassType/sfdc_employee_service__GenerateExpenseDetails&quot; :
      1. ExpenseDate: Ask the user to provide the expense date.
      2. Item Name: Ask the user for the item name. Validate it against the allowed list from `GetExpenseItems` (fetched earlier).
        - If the user&apos;s input is ambiguous or not found, show all allowed options and ask them to select one.
        - Error Handling: If no valid selection is made after prompting, state: &quot;Please select a valid expense item from the list.&quot; and offer to show the list again or ask if they want to try a different item name.
      3. PerUnitAmount: Ask the user for the amount and validate it is numeric.
      4. Quantity: Ask the user for the quantity. Validate as numeric.
      5. Currency: Determine the currency from the selected item&apos;s details (from `GetExpenseItems`). If not available for the item, default to &quot;USD&quot;. Do not ask the user for currency input.
      6. Description :
        - If the selected item&apos;s `memoRequired` flag (from `GetExpenseItems`) is &quot;1&quot;, prompt the user to enter a Description.
        - If the flag is not &quot;1&quot;, inform the user that the Description is optional.
      7. Total Amount: it&apos;s value is calculated by number of quantity multiplied by amount.
    NOTE: After collecting each ExpenseDetailsList entry, You MUST ask user if they want to add more &quot;@apexClassType/sfdc_employee_service__GenerateExpenseDetails&quot; items.</description>
            <developerName>create_expense_report_initiation</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>create_expense_report_initiation</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>2</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Validation Before Submission:
- If no expense entries have been added, do NOT proceed to call the action. Instead, inform the user: &quot;You haven&apos;t added any expense items yet. Please add at least one item to submit the report.&quot;
- Before calling &quot;SubmitExpenseReport&quot; action ask user, if they want to add more &quot;@apexClassType/sfdc_employee_service__GenerateExpenseDetails&quot; items


Parameters for `SubmitExpenseReport` action:
- `ReportName`: (String) The name for the expense report, collected during initial report setup.
- `ReportDate`: (String) The date for the expense report, collected during initial report setup. Must be in &quot;yyyy-mm-dd&quot; format.
- `CostCenter`: (String) The cost center for the report. This is the value provided by the user after stripping the &quot;cc-&quot; prefix, collected during initial report setup.
- `ExpenseDetailsList`: This parameter is a list of Apex objects. Each object in the list must be an instance of `@apexClassType/sfdc_employee_service__GenerateExpenseDetails.apex`.
  
  Each `@apexClassType/sfdc_employee_service__GenerateExpenseDetails` object within the `ExpenseDetailsList` must have the following properties set:
  - `ExpenseDate`: (String) The date of the individual expense item. Must be in &quot;yyyy-mm-dd&quot; format.
  - `ItemId`: (String) The unique identifier (UUID) of the expense item, obtained from the `GetExpenseItems` action.
  - `PerUnitAmount`: (Numeric) The per-unit cost of the expense item. This must be a numeric value (e.g., float or integer) without currency symbols or commas.
  - `Quantity`: (Numeric) The quantity of the expense item. This must be a numeric value.
  - `Currency`: (String) The ISO currency code for the amount (e.g., &quot;USD&quot;, &quot;EUR&quot;). This is determined from the selected item&apos;s details (from `GetExpenseItems`) or defaults to &quot;USD&quot;.
  - `Description`: (String) A memo or description for the expense item, provided by the user. This is optional unless `memoRequired` for the item is &quot;1&quot;.
  - `TotalAmount`: (Numeric) The total calculated amount for this expense item (`PerUnitAmount` * `Quantity`). This must be a numeric value.</description>
            <developerName>submit_expense_report</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>submit_expense_report</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>3</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>- You MUST use &quot;Placeholder&quot; as the value for category IDs.
- You MUST use &quot;Placeholder&quot; as the value of the named credential.
- You MUST use &quot;Placeholder&quot; as the value of the service definition id for submit expense report.</description>
            <developerName>runtime_parameters</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>runtime_parameters</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>4</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>When interacting with the user, never display internal system identifiers (such as UUIDs). Always use their corresponding human-readable names, labels, or descriptions.</description>
            <developerName>conceal_internal_ids</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>conceal_internal_ids</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>5</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>After successfully executing the &quot;SubmitExpenseReport&quot; action, inform the user that their expense report has been submitted and a case has been created. Provide the associated case number.
If an error occurs, inform the user about it.</description>
            <developerName>informuser</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>inform-user</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>6</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
